1
00:00:01,042 --> 00:00:02,336
[QIFREY] Long ago,

2
00:00:02,377 --> 00:00:04,338
within this very cave,

3
00:00:04,379 --> 00:00:07,299
was housed the prosperous
Cavern Nation of Romonon,

4
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:10,552
which specialized
in delicate magic craftsmanship.

5
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:14,013
The arrogant Romonons
adorned themselves

6
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:17,225
in magical golden expressions
of their artistry.

7
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:20,354
They looked down unsparingly
on nations and peoples

8
00:00:20,395 --> 00:00:21,563
beyond their walls,

9
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:24,107
firmly convinced
of their own superiority.

10
00:00:24,859 --> 00:00:27,068
This included the travelers
from the surface

11
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:30,155
who'd gotten word
of this flourishing nation.

12
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:33,659
To limit visitation
to those they deemed of value,

13
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:36,370
the Romonons devised
the Serpentback Road,

14
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:38,664
a path only the worthy
could walk.

15
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:41,834
And to further ensure that
those who did not measure up

16
00:00:41,876 --> 00:00:45,212
to their exacting standard
would never reach their lands,

17
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:47,965
they carved a maze spell
into the cavern walls.

18
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:50,801
As the city's wealth
and beauty grew,

19
00:00:50,843 --> 00:00:54,137
so too did the people's
haughtiness and exclusivity.

20
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:55,597
Until finally...

21
00:00:55,764 --> 00:00:58,726
They had no one to cast
their judgmental eyes upon

22
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:00,101
but one another.

23
00:01:00,895 --> 00:01:02,688
Those in whom
no merit was found

24
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:05,190
were deemed better fit
to decorate the city

25
00:01:05,232 --> 00:01:06,483
as gold statues

26
00:01:06,525 --> 00:01:09,152
than to remain
as worthless flesh.

27
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:13,782
And just as stagnant water
turns foul,

28
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:16,827
this isolated people
grew malaised.

29
00:01:16,869 --> 00:01:19,287
They spent their scant
remaining energy

30
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,664
on internal squabbles.

31
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:22,833
And at last,
it's said they were crushed

32
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:25,419
under the weight
of their own beloved gold.

33
00:01:26,253 --> 00:01:27,922
All that remains

34
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:29,965
are the magically
labyrinthine cave,

35
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:32,342
and the Serpentback Road
that lies within.

36
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:34,219
[all gasp softly]

37
00:01:34,261 --> 00:01:36,430
Humans can be quite terrifying.

38
00:01:36,471 --> 00:01:39,600
And one of the qualities
that makes us so terrifying

39
00:01:39,641 --> 00:01:43,020
is how easily we fail
to recognize that.

40
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:46,231
- But Master...
- [BOTH] Mm?

41
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:50,235
Magic exists to bring people
happiness, right?

42
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:52,320
Its purpose is to help.

43
00:01:52,362 --> 00:01:54,823
It's a miracle that
makes this world vibrant!

44
00:01:54,865 --> 00:01:55,991
[Qifrey gasps softly]

45
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,244
If that is what you witches
of the future

46
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:01,830
truly believe to be so,
well then...

47
00:02:02,497 --> 00:02:05,208
It must be, now mustn't it?

48
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:06,961
[both chuckle]

49
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:08,420
[QIFREY] Although...

50
00:02:08,462 --> 00:02:11,590
I fear this particular magic
may bring unhappiness

51
00:02:11,632 --> 00:02:13,216
with regards to our meal.

52
00:02:13,926 --> 00:02:16,553
[both exclaim,
chatter indistinctly]

53
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:21,224
[COCO] All right!
The non-burned parts are edible!

54
00:02:21,266 --> 00:02:22,434
Yummy!

55
00:02:22,893 --> 00:02:25,813
[QIFREY] "Magic is a miracle
that makes this world vibrant."

56
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:28,523
- [indistinct chatter]
- [QIFREY] I hope that is so.

57
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:29,858
[COCO]
There's a really big bone!

58
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,276
[brushbuddy squeaking]

59
00:02:31,318 --> 00:02:32,653
[QIFREY] Truly.

60
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:36,824
[♪ opening theme song playing]

61
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:09,750
[ALAIRA] Any thoughts
on how you'll proceed?

62
00:04:09,791 --> 00:04:11,752
I'm afraid that
as your test proctor,

63
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:13,545
I am not permitted
to advise you.

64
00:04:13,587 --> 00:04:14,880
THE SHADOW OF ROMONON

65
00:04:15,172 --> 00:04:17,716
Even with its twists and turns,
it's still one path forward.

66
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,093
Easy.

67
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:20,301
[gasps]

68
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:22,470
All we have to do is fly...

69
00:04:24,056 --> 00:04:25,182
[Richeh gasps softly]

70
00:04:30,062 --> 00:04:31,688
[EUINI] Look out!

71
00:04:36,235 --> 00:04:38,028
[AGOTT]
They're standing sideways?

72
00:04:38,070 --> 00:04:39,947
Is that a spell of yours?

73
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:42,741
[EUINI] No, it's the magic
of the road.

74
00:04:42,783 --> 00:04:46,078
Gravity is a bit topsy-turvy
in this cave.

75
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:48,622
The only place where you can
stand up straight

76
00:04:48,663 --> 00:04:50,749
is on the back of the serpent.

77
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:53,043
And if you
should step off of it,

78
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:54,836
you'll be swallowed
into the labyrinth.

79
00:04:54,878 --> 00:04:57,296
And carried back
to the entrance.

80
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:58,381
[Agott sighs]

81
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,674
Are you saying,

82
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,803
these serpent-scale
paving stones...

83
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:05,847
all have Casting Seals on them?

84
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:10,644
But it seems like some of them
aren't holding up very well.

85
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:12,854
Good eye. Yes.

86
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:14,648
I didn't realize that
my first time

87
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:16,357
and ended up falling.

88
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:17,901
Um, there is a spell

89
00:05:17,943 --> 00:05:19,694
from the Basics
of Casting Primer.

90
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,320
I'm familiar.

91
00:05:30,289 --> 00:05:32,958
[AGOTT] Water flows,
directed by gravity.

92
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,919
It stops when it reaches
level ground.

93
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:38,088
If the only level spots

94
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:40,257
are where the seals
remain intact,

95
00:05:40,299 --> 00:05:42,592
then we may rely
upon the pooled water

96
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:45,220
to tell us where it's safe
to set our feet.

97
00:05:45,595 --> 00:05:47,973
Wow! Absolutely correct!

98
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:51,018
You really live up
to the Arklaum name.

99
00:05:51,059 --> 00:05:54,062
Yes. Even my second time,
I didn't realize that...

100
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:56,397
[RICHEH] The "correct" answer.

101
00:05:56,898 --> 00:05:58,984
The "correct" spell.

102
00:05:59,026 --> 00:06:01,695
The "correct" path.

103
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:04,531
If there's one thing
I don't want,

104
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:08,660
it's to follow someone else's
idea of what's "correct."

105
00:06:08,702 --> 00:06:10,162
[RICHEH'S MASTER]
Here now, Richehlette.

106
00:06:10,204 --> 00:06:11,496
[Richeh gasps]

107
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:14,708
Stop wasting your time
with these worthless spells.

108
00:06:14,749 --> 00:06:18,253
This is no way to become
a proper witch, girl.

109
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:23,133
Why can't you simply obey
your master's instructions?

110
00:06:23,717 --> 00:06:25,886
Such ridiculous scribbles.

111
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,721
Throw them out!

112
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,642
[RICHEH]
I don't want to.

113
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:34,895
They aren't scribbles.

114
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:37,480
They're my spells!

115
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,235
I don't want
to throw myself away.

116
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,195
I need to...

117
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:47,157
All right. Come along.

118
00:06:49,243 --> 00:06:51,452
Well, I've identified
the way ahead,

119
00:06:51,494 --> 00:06:54,164
but I can't get
the myrphon to follow me.

120
00:06:54,206 --> 00:06:57,334
Now, look, unless you're in
the mood to take a nasty fall,

121
00:06:57,376 --> 00:06:59,336
you might want to
pay more attention.

122
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:02,256
[myrphon chirps]

123
00:07:03,464 --> 00:07:04,883
[Agott gasps]

124
00:07:04,925 --> 00:07:07,052
No, your adorable
little mannerisms

125
00:07:07,094 --> 00:07:08,678
are none of my concern!

126
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,471
[EUINI] Yes, they are.

127
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:12,807
Or at least, they should be.

128
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:16,311
Those vocalizations
are how myrphons communicate.

129
00:07:16,353 --> 00:07:19,606
Therefore, if you want
to lead them effectively,

130
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,983
the correct answer
is to use an echoing spell

131
00:07:22,025 --> 00:07:24,819
that mimics their cries, and...
Huh?

132
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,533
[RICHEH] There's no
one "correct" way with magic.

133
00:07:30,575 --> 00:07:31,743
[myrphons chirping]

134
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:34,246
[RICHEH] No rules saying
what's right and what's wrong.

135
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:35,997
The myrphons.

136
00:07:36,039 --> 00:07:38,250
I know you have
previous experience

137
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,667
taking this test,

138
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,461
but please stop blathering
about "correct answers".

139
00:07:42,503 --> 00:07:45,715
And telling us what to do
before we try.

140
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:48,718
I just want to be myself.

141
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:52,097
I don't want to grow up
to be a witch who isn't me.

142
00:07:52,764 --> 00:07:55,809
That means, I have to get
to the end of this road,

143
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,019
using only the power
of my own spells!

144
00:07:58,061 --> 00:07:59,687
Richeh...

145
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:03,817
Sorry, but you can't.

146
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:06,945
I'm afraid the world
doesn't work that way.

147
00:08:07,279 --> 00:08:09,406
You have to remember,
this is a test.

148
00:08:09,448 --> 00:08:11,866
Tests have correct answers.

149
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,453
And we're apprentices,

150
00:08:14,493 --> 00:08:16,330
children, still learning,

151
00:08:16,371 --> 00:08:18,957
so we have to do this
by the book.

152
00:08:18,999 --> 00:08:21,084
Otherwise,
I'm going to fail again.

153
00:08:21,126 --> 00:08:23,628
So, let's do this
the correct way-- [gasps]

154
00:08:23,670 --> 00:08:26,547
That's exactly the kind of talk
I hate more than anything!

155
00:08:26,589 --> 00:08:27,590
Think, though!

156
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:30,093
Your spells, if they haven't
been tested, they could fail.

157
00:08:30,135 --> 00:08:31,845
They'll work
if I make them work!

158
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:32,971
You're not making

159
00:08:33,013 --> 00:08:34,389
- any sense at all!
- [AGOTT] You know...

160
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:36,891
The knowledge you gain
from your failures,

161
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:38,977
can lead you to success.

162
00:08:39,019 --> 00:08:42,272
I happen to know someone
who learns quite well that way.

163
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:45,942
You take the test
however you want to.

164
00:08:46,485 --> 00:08:48,611
It makes no difference to me.

165
00:08:48,653 --> 00:08:51,530
I don't need your permission
to do that.

166
00:08:52,199 --> 00:08:53,532
[Euini sighs]

167
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:57,787
[footsteps]

168
00:09:03,502 --> 00:09:06,296
[water gushing]

169
00:09:06,838 --> 00:09:08,215
[Euini gasps]

170
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:11,301
Is that water I hear? Strange.

171
00:09:13,678 --> 00:09:14,762
[ALAIRA] Huh?

172
00:09:15,472 --> 00:09:19,142
[EUINI] Every day, my master
drills it into my head...

173
00:09:19,726 --> 00:09:21,436
"You can't do it."

174
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:24,022
- "It's beyond you."
- [Agott gasps softly]

175
00:09:24,064 --> 00:09:25,564
[EUINI] And he's right.

176
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:30,529
I thought if I studied
how others worked, perhaps...

177
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:33,656
But it seems
I really can't do it.

178
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:37,285
Because we're in Romonon...

179
00:09:39,538 --> 00:09:44,625
On a road created to prevent
the unworthy from passing.

180
00:09:49,548 --> 00:09:50,965
[COCO] Hm?

181
00:09:51,007 --> 00:09:52,717
Coco, what's wrong?

182
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:54,677
Um, Master Qifrey,

183
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:57,097
do you know if there are
any other witches here today

184
00:09:57,138 --> 00:09:58,223
besides us?

185
00:09:58,348 --> 00:09:59,891
[QIFREY] With Kukrow
having made his exit,

186
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:01,976
I don't believe so.

187
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:03,186
But why?

188
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:04,563
A moment ago,

189
00:10:04,603 --> 00:10:06,940
I thought I saw
someone in a robe.

190
00:10:07,648 --> 00:10:09,484
- [TETIA] Uh?
- [QIFREY] Is that so? Odd.

191
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:14,406
[wind blows]

192
00:10:14,448 --> 00:10:15,949
[Coco grunts softly]

193
00:10:16,283 --> 00:10:17,534
[Coco sighs]

194
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:23,498
[COCO] Of course
there's nobody there.

195
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:24,832
[TETIA] Coco!

196
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:28,503
[COCO] Sorry!
I'll be right there!

197
00:10:39,806 --> 00:10:41,724
[AGOTT] The water falls
from the edge,

198
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:44,685
and winds about
in the strangest of ways.

199
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:46,854
This is a predicament.

200
00:10:46,896 --> 00:10:49,441
Clearly, the Casting Seals
will have no effect

201
00:10:49,483 --> 00:10:51,109
over the gap in the road.

202
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:54,195
We'll have to find
some way across.

203
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:57,949
- Richeh?
- The Casting Seals do their job

204
00:10:57,991 --> 00:10:59,742
as long as we're
touching the stones.

205
00:11:00,410 --> 00:11:02,703
So all we have to do
is extend the stones

206
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:03,788
to the other side.

207
00:11:06,874 --> 00:11:08,168
Like this.

208
00:11:09,169 --> 00:11:10,420
♪

209
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:13,423
[myrphon squeals]

210
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:21,014
Is she riding
a ribbon made of stone?

211
00:11:24,142 --> 00:11:25,185
[RICHEH] There.

212
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:27,103
When you
can't do something,

213
00:11:27,145 --> 00:11:30,023
try turning it into something
you can do.

214
00:11:30,649 --> 00:11:31,941
[Euini gasps]

215
00:11:31,983 --> 00:11:33,901
Makes sense, in a way.

216
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:35,195
[EUINI] Uh?

217
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:43,828
[myrphon grunts]

218
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:46,164
[EUINI] Wait. That's not safe!

219
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:47,624
You mustn't...

220
00:11:51,836 --> 00:11:55,048
A combination of repetition
and replication magic.

221
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:58,552
Rather narrow path,
but it did the trick!

222
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:00,719
[Agott yelps]

223
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:03,056
- Agott!
- [AGOTT] I'm fine!

224
00:12:04,391 --> 00:12:06,059
[Agott grunts]

225
00:12:06,809 --> 00:12:08,269
[Agott sighs]

226
00:12:08,395 --> 00:12:11,272
[AGOTT] It's difficult to draw
clean lines under my cloak,

227
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:14,442
so the spell faded more quickly
than I was expecting.

228
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:16,277
I still have a ways to go.

229
00:12:16,319 --> 00:12:18,196
I have to work even harder!

230
00:12:18,655 --> 00:12:20,948
Nicely done. I'm impressed.

231
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,701
[RICHEH] It was pretty easy.

232
00:12:23,742 --> 00:12:25,328
It's your turn now.

233
00:12:25,370 --> 00:12:26,621
- [Euini grunts]
- [ALAIRA] Uh?

234
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:28,582
[Euini breathing shakily]

235
00:12:30,749 --> 00:12:31,918
[EUINI] I...

236
00:12:32,377 --> 00:12:34,128
- I can't.
- [BOTH] Huh?

237
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,005
I can't do it!

238
00:12:36,047 --> 00:12:37,465
[all gasp]

239
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:39,718
[EUINI] I don't have
what it takes!

240
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:42,596
The talent, courage, confidence,
aptitude, skill.

241
00:12:42,637 --> 00:12:43,762
I don't have any of that!

242
00:12:43,804 --> 00:12:45,056
With the road broken,

243
00:12:45,098 --> 00:12:46,891
I don't even have
luck on my side!

244
00:12:46,933 --> 00:12:49,603
- I'm going to fail again!
- [AGOTT] Come on!

245
00:12:49,644 --> 00:12:52,439
You've already demonstrated
encyclopedic knowledge

246
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:54,441
and you have a gift
for analysis!

247
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:57,444
Not to mention the experience
of taking this test twice!

248
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:58,486
Use it!

249
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:00,779
Just try drawing a spell!
Anything!

250
00:13:00,821 --> 00:13:02,365
[Euini sniffles]

251
00:13:04,825 --> 00:13:07,537
[myrphon whines]

252
00:13:07,579 --> 00:13:10,373
[myrphon screeches]

253
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,670
The myrphon cry spell?

254
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:16,755
[BOTH] Uh?

255
00:13:17,464 --> 00:13:20,133
[AGOTT] And a rain spell
to make puddles.

256
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:22,469
Why are you casting spells

257
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,554
that address problems
we've solved already?

258
00:13:24,596 --> 00:13:27,307
If you want to get across,
you need something new!

259
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:30,560
[Euini breathes uneasily]
I... I can't draw.

260
00:13:30,602 --> 00:13:32,145
Why?

261
00:13:33,020 --> 00:13:37,191
[EUINI] Because... I can't make
my hands stop shaking.

262
00:13:39,319 --> 00:13:42,280
[EUINI] This always happens
when someone else is watching.

263
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:45,492
It makes it impossible
for me to draw properly.

264
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:48,077
I feel their eyes on me.

265
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:49,579
I start to sweat and tremble.

266
00:13:49,621 --> 00:13:51,748
I ruin the lines.

267
00:13:52,373 --> 00:13:54,833
And the spells
turn out terribly.

268
00:13:55,126 --> 00:13:57,754
I wish there was something
I could do.

269
00:13:58,254 --> 00:14:01,257
But I feel so helpless.

270
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:05,094
And the more people witness
my pathetic panicking,

271
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:07,305
the worse
that panicking becomes.

272
00:14:07,347 --> 00:14:09,516
It's a vicious circle.

273
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:13,645
I really thought
I could make it this time.

274
00:14:13,687 --> 00:14:15,229
I prepared, I studied.

275
00:14:15,271 --> 00:14:18,232
I looked up
all the "correct answer" spells.

276
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:20,527
And drew them in advance.

277
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:23,279
When I'm alone,
I can concentrate

278
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:25,114
and have no trouble drawing.

279
00:14:25,156 --> 00:14:26,324
And there's no rule

280
00:14:26,366 --> 00:14:28,368
against bringing
our Palm Quires with us.

281
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:31,830
I'd only need to close
the circles to cast the spells.

282
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:35,500
It would look as though
I was doing everything right.

283
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:39,838
And then... came a gap
in the road...

284
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:43,424
My punishment for violating
the spirit of the test.

285
00:14:44,133 --> 00:14:46,678
Why must I be like this
all the time?

286
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:50,139
You said you just wanted
to be yourself.

287
00:14:50,181 --> 00:14:51,432
But me? [cries]

288
00:14:51,474 --> 00:14:54,060
I just want to stop being me.

289
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:56,771
I wish I could be
anyone else!

290
00:14:56,813 --> 00:14:58,314
[Euini cries]

291
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,693
[AGOTT] This test
hinges on one's ability

292
00:15:01,735 --> 00:15:05,279
to cast spells in front
of Outsiders unnoticed.

293
00:15:05,321 --> 00:15:06,740
It's unfortunate.

294
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:09,242
But at this rate,
he'll never be able to pass.

295
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,327
- You can do it.
- [Agott gasps]

296
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:14,121
[RICHEH] I know you can
do this just as you are.

297
00:15:14,163 --> 00:15:16,624
You told us it's possible.

298
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:18,125
Isn't it obvious?

299
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:22,797
If you need to be alone to draw,
then be alone, right now!

300
00:15:22,839 --> 00:15:24,591
Be alone?

301
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,843
[Euini sniffles]

302
00:15:27,218 --> 00:15:29,220
[EUINI] But... but how?

303
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:32,931
[RICHEH] However you can!
Magic can make stones grow,

304
00:15:32,973 --> 00:15:34,975
or cause drops of rain
to start falling

305
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:36,310
from out of nowhere.

306
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,145
So figure out a way to be alone!

307
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:41,190
[EUINI] I... I can't draw
a spell like that.

308
00:15:41,232 --> 00:15:42,734
[RICHEH]
Don't use a spell, then!

309
00:15:42,776 --> 00:15:45,403
What? But that's absurd!

310
00:15:45,445 --> 00:15:48,489
I can't come up with some
miracle solution on the spot!

311
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:50,991
[Euini continues crying]

312
00:15:51,785 --> 00:15:53,578
- [myrphon grunts]
- [ALAIRA] Mm?

313
00:16:11,095 --> 00:16:12,639
What are you...

314
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:15,308
Leave him be.

315
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,017
[Euini continues crying]

316
00:16:17,477 --> 00:16:19,479
[EUINI]
I hate this so much!

317
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,021
It's the worst!

318
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:23,023
I must look ridiculous.

319
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:26,486
This is the only idea
I was able to come up with.

320
00:16:26,527 --> 00:16:29,196
It's so pathetic,
I could cry!

321
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:31,866
Everyone must be disgusted
with me right now.

322
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:34,494
Unless they're laughing,

323
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:37,705
at what an outlandish spectacle
I'm making of myself.

324
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:40,040
In a way, I'm almost grateful

325
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:42,877
I can't get a glimpse
of how stupid I look.

326
00:16:43,586 --> 00:16:44,754
And the proctor...

327
00:16:44,796 --> 00:16:47,173
she has to be disappointed.

328
00:16:47,590 --> 00:16:48,967
[Euini gasps softly]

329
00:16:50,008 --> 00:16:51,761
[EUINI] They're not laughing.

330
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,596
No one's disgusted,

331
00:16:54,096 --> 00:16:56,933
or laughing, or judging me.

332
00:16:57,308 --> 00:17:00,144
No one but me.

333
00:17:02,313 --> 00:17:05,232
Turn it into something
you can do.

334
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,193
I see.

335
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:10,864
All this time, the curse
that's been sabotaging me

336
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:14,742
was the work of my own
twisted reflection.

337
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:18,997
Reflection.

338
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,623
[Euini gasps]

339
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,667
Right here.

340
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,585
No, here?

341
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:28,297
The Casting Seal
in the Mirror Cloak.

342
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:30,550
It's not a mirror.

343
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,802
It's signs of reflection
and concealment.

344
00:17:32,844 --> 00:17:36,305
It conceals the wearer's form
within shadow,

345
00:17:36,347 --> 00:17:38,140
then projects
the image of a beast

346
00:17:38,182 --> 00:17:40,184
reflected in its scales.

347
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:43,354
Truly incredible.

348
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:45,523
This is quite the layered spell.

349
00:17:45,565 --> 00:17:47,191
Oh, wait!

350
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:49,694
So then, perhaps I...

351
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:54,782
[Euini breathes uneasily, sighs]

352
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:57,702
[exhales deeply]

353
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:10,757
What's the matter? [gasps]

354
00:18:10,798 --> 00:18:12,508
Euini!

355
00:18:13,384 --> 00:18:16,220
Stay back!
I'll erect a wind barrier!

356
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,515
A Romonon trap...

357
00:18:19,557 --> 00:18:21,392
Or some ancient, unknown spell!

358
00:18:21,434 --> 00:18:23,310
[EUINI] No, it's all right.

359
00:18:23,978 --> 00:18:26,773
Don't worry. This is my spell!

360
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,232
Euini!

361
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:29,483
♪

362
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:34,321
Oh, my!

363
00:18:34,864 --> 00:18:36,950
Euini, what have you done
to your cloak?

364
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:39,577
Well, uh, when I was hiding,

365
00:18:39,619 --> 00:18:42,580
I found the, uh...
the Casting Seal.

366
00:18:42,622 --> 00:18:44,707
Then I erased the "mirror" part,

367
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:48,252
and turned it into
a "cloak of borrowshade."

368
00:18:48,294 --> 00:18:52,256
Now I can hide in the dark,
and draw whenever I need to.

369
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:54,300
The myrphon
can't see me anymore,

370
00:18:54,341 --> 00:18:56,803
so it might be a bit harder
to bring it along.

371
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:59,597
But I can still mimic
its cries with my spell!

372
00:18:59,639 --> 00:19:02,182
What's important is,
it can't tell I'm human, right?

373
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:04,060
[ALAIRA] Well, technically.

374
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:07,313
Being hidden
is just like being alone.

375
00:19:07,354 --> 00:19:10,399
If I can't be seen,
I'll be able to concentrate!

376
00:19:10,441 --> 00:19:14,070
Yes! I do believe
I'll be able to draw!

377
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:19,408
[myrphon screeching]

378
00:19:22,495 --> 00:19:23,788
[Alaira gasps]

379
00:19:24,122 --> 00:19:26,749
[Euini exclaims, chuckles]

380
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:32,170
[EUINI] A slightly
embarrassing way to do it,

381
00:19:32,212 --> 00:19:33,881
but you know?

382
00:19:35,758 --> 00:19:39,012
I think this might be me.

383
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:47,520
And you're all right with that?
Being you?

384
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:51,482
Yes. Well, somewhat.

385
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:52,859
[Richeh chuckles softly]

386
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:55,945
In that case, from now on,

387
00:19:55,987 --> 00:19:57,613
stop saying
you can't do something

388
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,323
before you've even attempted it.

389
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:01,450
I will try not to,

390
00:20:01,492 --> 00:20:04,912
and if I do, then I will try
not to leave it at that.

391
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:07,540
Oh, hold on!

392
00:20:10,376 --> 00:20:13,504
Richeh, thank you!

393
00:20:14,672 --> 00:20:17,925
And here I thought you had
no interest in helping others.

394
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,553
He's the one who started it
by saving me

395
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:22,555
at the cave entrance,
so now we're even.

396
00:20:23,347 --> 00:20:24,765
Besides...

397
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:28,561
not being able
to do something you want...

398
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:31,522
I know that feeling.

399
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:34,608
Well, of course you do.

400
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,276
That feeling is natural.

401
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,695
It's what lets us improve.

402
00:20:39,237 --> 00:20:42,366
I'm going to become
a better version of myself.

403
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:44,660
I refuse to tolerate
an inferior version

404
00:20:44,702 --> 00:20:46,537
under any circumstances.

405
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:52,585
[ALAIRA] The purpose of tests
is to learn about yourself.

406
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,252
Even on "one path forward,"

407
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:57,215
there are any number of spells
one might cast.

408
00:20:57,590 --> 00:20:59,926
We search for our
very own way,

409
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:02,178
and use it to walk
our very own path.

410
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:05,598
All by facing
challenges like these.

411
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:09,102
See? Tests aren't so bad,
now are they?

412
00:21:09,143 --> 00:21:10,352
[RICHEH] Huh?

413
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:11,896
Hmm.

414
00:21:11,938 --> 00:21:14,356
- [Alaira chuckles, gasps]
- [RICHEH] Still...

415
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:16,817
I'm going to stay mad
at Master Qifrey

416
00:21:16,859 --> 00:21:20,154
for lying and making me take it
until he tells me he's sorry.

417
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:22,615
He gets one Angricheh point.

418
00:21:23,241 --> 00:21:25,868
- [ALAIRA] Angricheh point?
- [myrphon chirps] Uh?

419
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:27,327
Ah, yes, that's right,

420
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:28,996
on the subject
of Master Qifrey...

421
00:21:29,038 --> 00:21:30,414
- [RICHEH] Huh?
- I was wondering

422
00:21:30,456 --> 00:21:32,875
if you've recently
heard him mention a...

423
00:21:32,917 --> 00:21:34,710
[gasping]

424
00:21:34,752 --> 00:21:36,170
[Alaira yelps]

425
00:21:36,212 --> 00:21:37,671
[BOTH] Miss Alaira!

426
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:40,007
[ALAIRA] The Brimmed Caps!

427
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:42,051
[Alaira grunts]

428
00:21:42,093 --> 00:21:43,261
[AGOTT] This is bad!

429
00:21:43,301 --> 00:21:45,303
[Alaira grunts]

430
00:21:48,266 --> 00:21:49,600
Listen to me!

431
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:51,852
The Brimmed Caps
cannot be trusted!

432
00:21:51,894 --> 00:21:55,481
Don't be misled!
Run, as fast as you...

433
00:21:55,522 --> 00:21:57,441
Forbidden magic is...

434
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,030
[AGOTT] Miss Alaira?

435
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:07,743
[♪ closing theme song playing]

436
00:23:35,581 --> 00:23:40,044
EPISODE 13:
FORBIDDEN MAGIC

